{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Input seals x25519-xc20p-input (spec §3.11, ADR 0004): a secret value typed into the /input form, sealed to the one-time input_pub that one online device issued for one input request. epk = X25519(ephemeral_secret, 9); shared = X25519(ephemeral_secret, input_pub) (all-zero: bad_request); key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=shared, salt=epk || input_pub, info=utf8(\"akv1/input-seal\"), L=32); aad = cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/input-seal\",\"request_id\",\"vault_id\",\"account\",\"device_id\",\"name\",\"purpose\" (null when absent),\"operation\",\"expires_at\"}) from context; ct = XChaCha20-Poly1305(key, n, cjson(payload), aad); payload = {\"value\", \"sensitivity\"?}. cases: sealInput(input_pub, context, payload) with the given ephemeral_secret and nonce wire.n MUST reproduce wire byte for byte, and openInput(input_secret, wire, context) MUST yield payload. openInput order: parse (v or alg unknown: unsupported_version; exact keys, request_id ID, epk 32 B, n 24 B, ct 16..65552 B: bad_request); wire.request_id other than context.request_id (bad_request); all-zero shared secret (bad_request); AEAD failure (decrypt_failed); pt not canonical, no value, unknown keys, value not a string or over 65536 UTF-16 code units, unknown sensitivity (bad_request). invalid: openInput(input_secret, wire, context) MUST fail with expect_error; a case with ct_zero_bytes replaces wire.ct with that many zero bytes. seal_invalid: sealInput MUST refuse context and payload with expect_error; value_fill sets payload.value to value_fill repeated value_length times.",
